{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/48824-pacts-and-supernatural-merits","id":48824,"title":"Pacts and supernatural merits.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-14T02:49:44-08:00","id":48824,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon4.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Pacts and supernatural merits.","content":"Question about some of the Merits provided by a pact. Could a demon, for example, provide a Familiar vie a pact or give a mortal psychomancy or the like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1991-fallenxanderel","name":"FallenXanderel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T06:36:38-08:00","id":48917,"title":"","content":"I'd allow it. Demons provided supernatural power is very much in-theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T18:00:49-08:00","id":49399,"title":"","content":"Would said pact result in the signer becoming a stigmatic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2001-tyler-foss","name":"Tyler Foss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T08:49:46-08:00","id":49839,"title":"","content":"And how about doing the same thing for supernatural creatures? Could a pact grant blood potency or devotion? Could they grant a contract use?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T09:49:18-08:00","id":49866,"title":"","content":"This topic raises another interesting question. When a Demon gets bits and pieces of a supernatural's identity that are not supernatural in themselves, is the bit supernatural or mundane when the Demon claims it?<br /> <br /> Let's say a vampire has a Mask of &quot;Artist&quot; and haggles that away in a Pact, if the Demon adds it to a Patchwork cover, is that &quot;vampiric artist&quot; or &quot;artist&quot; ?<br /> <br /> Or if a mage who still has contact with his Sleeper family gives away his unloved third cousin, is that &quot;unloved cousin of the mage Hermes-Toth&quot; or &quot; unloved cousin of David Simmons&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T12:43:28-08:00","id":49992,"title":"","content":"When a demon takes a piece of a life through a pact it edits out the old person and writes in the demon. So that unloved 3rd cousin is, for all intents and purposes, the demon's cousin now, and to the extent that the pact rewrites things, he always was.<br /> <br /> As far as the Mask, it pretty clearly spells out that when a demon takes stuff from a supernatural through pact that they get normal mortal versions of it. The example was taking a vampire's identity as a Cover through a soul pact. The demon gets all the social connections and the physical appearance of the vampire, but this Cover is a normal mortal with no vampiric traits or abilities, just like any other Cover would be. Plus, since a Mask represents the vampire's masquerade it'll likely have a lot of normal mortal interconnections. If the demon were to take a vampire's Dirge through a pact that could get interesting.<br /> <br /> With regard to actual supernatural power use, it seems thematic for demonic pacts granting actual, tangible power, but the scope of such pacts could get out of hand fairly quickly. You could do something quick and dirty if you want to use it. Say, Lesser aspect granting 1 dot of a power, Medial granting 2 or increasing an existing one by 1, and Greater granting 3 or increasing an existing by 2. That's a good bit of equivalent experience and relative power level, though (5 experiences for a Greater pact granting a 5 dot merit, versus 12 experiences for a Greater pact granting a 3 dot out of clan discipline).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T15:33:17-08:00","id":50162,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't let Demons give splat-based powers, their occult physic powers don't really extend into that territory. The reason they give Supernatural merits is those are deliberately possible within the scope of the God-Machine and its occult physics. Those physics don't make the Supernal any more than they make the Beast, which come from Other Things/Places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T18:04:15-08:00","id":50299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/48824-pacts-and-supernatural-merits?p=49992#post49992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as the Mask, it pretty clearly spells out that when a demon takes stuff from a supernatural through pact that they get normal mortal versions of it. The example was taking a vampire's identity as a Cover through a soul pact. The demon gets all the social connections and the physical appearance of the vampire, but this Cover is a normal mortal with no vampiric traits or abilities, just like any other Cover would be. Plus, since a Mask represents the vampire's masquerade it'll likely have a lot of normal mortal interconnections. If the demon were to take a vampire's Dirge through a pact that could get interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I already knew all of that but reading your response made me think of two questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>So once you take the Vampire identity, you could look as pale as the vamp looked at the moment the pact was enacted. But soon blood would begin to color the Cover's skin. I'd think that the cover's friends or just those who have seen it before would notice and think that that vampire has turned human. I guess this really isn't a question, just a thought on an interesting Plot hook for a vampire game: One of the Coterie's acquaintances &quot;turns&quot; human and all of the implications of that. (to keep it as non cross-overy as possible I would not actually make it overtly obvious it was a demon to keep the story interesting.</li> <li>I forgot the other actually real question so I'll use this as a placeholder for later when I think of it.</li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T22:21:05-08:00","id":50440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/48824-pacts-and-supernatural-merits?p=50299#post50299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So I already knew all of that but reading your response made me think of two questions: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>So once you take the Vampire identity, you could look as pale as the vamp looked at the moment the pact was enacted. But soon blood would begin to color the Cover's skin. I'd think that the cover's friends or just those who have seen it before would notice and think that that vampire has turned human. I guess this really isn't a question, just a thought on an interesting Plot hook for a vampire game: One of the Coterie's acquaintances &quot;turns&quot; human and all of the implications of that. (to keep it as non cross-overy as possible I would not actually make it overtly obvious it was a demon to keep the story interesting.</li> <li>I forgot the other actually real question so I'll use this as a placeholder for later when I think of it.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>That bit about Mask/Dirge was directed at Saibot, sorry for the confusion. I got lazy and didn't use quotes to respond directly.<br /> <br /> As for #1 there, that's actually a really fun idea. Shamelessly stolen for when my Requiem game kicks back up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T05:51:18-08:00","id":50600,"title":"","content":"Oh right! I remember #2!:<br /> <br /> What happens to a vamp's Mask or Dirge if it is taken by pact? does the mask or dirge shift to a new one or how would that work for the vampire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T07:05:56-08:00","id":50649,"title":"","content":"I was pondering that myself in the wake of all this business. I'll have to reread the pacts section, but now that I look at it more closely an entire Mask or Dirge seems a little too complex to be sold off with anything less than a soul pact. <br /> <br /> There are a whole lot of little pieces that go into making up a vampire's identity. The Mask represents every little facet of how they present their face to the living world, so that's just chock full of mortal-focused social merits, acquaintances, business associates, customers, patrons, etc. Each one of those things represents something a demon takes with a pact's aspects. It's just too much to sell all at once unless you completely sell out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T13:23:04-08:00","id":55650,"title":"","content":"Demons operate by modifying fundamental values of the Universe around them. The GM has set up very specific rules for how the world works: Someone (Resources 1) dies and their money is sloughed off to different places to pay off debters, fees, taxes, etc. Now imagine how many people die every day. Demons hack the underlying code of the universe so that when someone dies, their Resources are reallocated as the Demon sees fit. Remember the movie Office Space? The Demon just rewrites where the floating decimals worth of Resources go for all the people that die in the next while, funneling it towards the new recipient. <br /> <br /> That being said, there are two fundamental questions needing answers before we can say whether Demons can use this same hackery to affect supernatural values.<br /> <br /> A) Does the Demon in question understand how the value of the Supernatural trait functions? <br /> <br /> Demons are no more aware of the how and why of other races than other races are of Demon. But, different STs may allow varied levels of discovery in regards to those traits.<br /> <br /> B) Is the Supernatural Trait in question similar enough that it has a tangible value in the universe?<br /> <br /> If someone with this Supernatural Trait dies, what happens to the resulting energy? This is, of course, assuming that Death is the only way to lose values of, say, a Power Stat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2074-64bitjedi","name":"64bitjedi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T00:22:39-08:00","id":57958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/48824-pacts-and-supernatural-merits?p=50299#post50299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So I already knew all of that but reading your response made me think of two questions: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>So once you take the Vampire identity, you could look as pale as the vamp looked at the moment the pact was enacted. But soon blood would begin to color the Cover's skin. I'd think that the cover's friends or just those who have seen it before would notice and think that that vampire has turned human. I guess this really isn't a question, just a thought on an interesting Plot hook for a vampire game: One of the Coterie's acquaintances &quot;turns&quot; human and all of the implications of that. (to keep it as non cross-overy as possible I would not actually make it overtly obvious it was a demon to keep the story interesting.</li> <li>I forgot the other actually real question so I'll use this as a placeholder for later when I think of it.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>If the vampire was low on blood during that time it could be that the new cover will be pale and stay pale (and suffer from anaemia......that would fit with the current situation of the vampire even without supernatural properties included he was low on blood)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T09:46:22-08:00","id":58143,"title":"","content":"So, I think it's important to point out here that, in the book, in the section on pacts, it says more than once that Demons don't actually know how pacts WORK.<br /> They know they DO work, and they know (instinctively) how to make them and what the rules for balancing them are, but the Demon doesn't actually MAKE the pact work, know WHERE or HOW the benefit comes from, nor do they decide any of these things, beyond simply agreeing to the pact and signing it with the mortal.<br /> <br /> So a Demon makes a pact with a Mortal. In exchange for the persons First Born Child (Greater relationship - Cover - +3) Permanently (duration +3), the Demon grants the Mortal Wealth (Greater Asset - Resources increased by three dots - +3) Permanently (duration +3). <br /> Mechanically - The Demon gains 3 cover XP and a free child, while the mortal's net worth jumps from middle class to Bill Gates esque. <br /> Now, reality, undirected by the Demon, Balances the scales. Somewhere, another mortal or group of mortals LOSE resources. But the demon doesn't decide WHO. Or HOW they lose those resources. <br /> <br /> Relevant pages: p 189, under Pacts, 3rd and 4th paragraphs; p 192 'Where does the Money Come From' sidebar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T10:09:07-08:00","id":58158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/48824-pacts-and-supernatural-merits?p=50600#post50600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh right! I remember #2!:<br /> <br /> What happens to a vamp's Mask or Dirge if it is taken by pact? does the mask or dirge shift to a new one or how would that work for the vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div> Can a pact mess with a mortal's Virtue and Vice like that? If so, then probably the same thing happens with vamps. <br /> <br /> Pacts are made to benefit either party. There's no benefit to either party by taking Mask, Dirge, Virtue, Vice, or whatever; a Pact would take the connections that derive from a vampire's Dirge or Mask, but taking anyone's ability to regain willpower from indulging something? <br /> <br /> I mean, how would you even WORD such a thing in a deal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T11:42:30-08:00","id":58213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/48824-pacts-and-supernatural-merits?p=58143#post58143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I think it's important to point out here that, in the book, in the section on pacts, it says more than once that Demons don't actually know how pacts WORK. They know they DO work, and they know (instinctively) how to make them and what the rules for balancing them are, but the Demon doesn't actually MAKE the pact work, know WHERE or HOW the benefit comes from, nor do they decide any of these things, beyond simply agreeing to the pact and signing it with the mortal. So a Demon makes a pact with a Mortal. In exchange for the persons First Born Child (Greater relationship - Cover - +3) Permanently (duration +3), the Demon grants the Mortal Wealth (Greater Asset - Resources increased by three dots - +3) Permanently (duration +3). Mechanically - The Demon gains 3 cover XP and a free child, while the mortal's net worth jumps from middle class to Bill Gates esque. Now, reality, undirected by the Demon, Balances the scales. Somewhere, another mortal or group of mortals LOSE resources. But the demon doesn't decide WHO. Or HOW they lose those resources. Relevant pages: p 189, under Pacts, 3rd and 4th paragraphs; p 192 'Where does the Money Come From' sidebar</div> </div> </div> </div> I believe (at work so AFPDF) that duration factors are only applied once, on the demon side of the scale. So your pact is three points in the demon's favor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T01:50:10-08:00","id":58588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/48824-pacts-and-supernatural-merits?p=49839#post49839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how about doing the same thing for supernatural creatures? Could a pact grant blood potency or devotion? Could they grant a contract use?</div> </div> </div> </div>My first inclination is to disallow pacts to grant supernatural potency, like Blood Potency or Primal Urge.<br /> <br /> But then I think, &quot;Would this be interesting?&quot; Yes, yes it would. For that matter, it's not like the demon is actually transforming you <i>into </i>a supernatural creature. She's simply pulling from the cosmos to enhance something already present. It leads to possibilities like vampires signing pacts with demons for power, and not just the temporal kind. That's something I like. However, I am not sure if I'd go so far as to allow the granting of various powers. It, too, leads to fun options, but might be pushing things a bit. This is one that is probably up to individual groups.<br /> <br /> The idea of a demon and changeling signing a contract to <i>use </i>a Contract is ... amusing. I'm trying to imagine the metaphysical legal tangle that would result in demonic pacts meeting ancient Fae bargains with reality itself.<br /> <br /> <i>Something</i> will explode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T13:44:12-08:00","id":65104,"title":"","content":"I agree that it would be up to individual groups, but I would think that an increase in either available powers or potency would cost at least as much as one for a human soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}